    explanation: "This problem gives the interviewer a quick way to judge how the candidate reasons about reason about palindromes in a way that is both correct and explainable. A strong response should make the core invariant, the important edge cases, and the complexity visible so the interviewer can distinguish genuine understanding from memorized code. The supplied source attributes this item to Reported by: Amazon SDE1; Amazon interview experience. Sources cited in the original file.",
    sampleAnswer: "For the longest palindromic substring, expand around every possible center. Each character is a center for an odd-length palindrome, and each gap is a center for an even-length palindrome. Expand while the characters match and retain the longest range. The straightforward solution is O(n2) time and O(1) auxiliary space; Manacher's algorithm can reduce the time to O(n), but it is usually unnecessary unless the constraints demand it.\n\nA concise implementation is shown in the detailed answer.",
    detailedAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nFor the longest palindromic substring, expand around every possible center. Each character is a center for an odd-length palindrome, and each gap is a center for an even-length palindrome. Expand while the characters match and retain the longest range. The straightforward solution is O(n2) time and O(1) auxiliary space; Manacher's algorithm can reduce the time to O(n), but it is usually unnecessary unless the constraints demand it.\n\n**Implementation example:**\n\n```python\ndef longest_palindrome(s):\n    best = \"\"\n    def expand(l, r):\n        while l >= 0 and r < len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:\n            l -= 1\n            r += 1\n        return s[l + 1:r]\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        for l, r in ((i, i), (i, i + 1)):\n            p = expand(l, r)\n            if len(p) > len(best):\n                best = p\n    return best\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\nFor 'babad', 'bab' and 'aba' are both valid longest palindromic substrings; the algorithm only needs to return one longest answer. The example is deliberately focused on the specific interview topic in entry 18.",
