    sampleAnswer: "Use recursion to remove the top element until the stack is empty. Then insert each removed element at the bottom while the recursive calls return. The key helper is insertAtBottom, which temporarily removes elements until the bottom is reached. This uses O(n2) time in the straightforward implementation and O(n) call-stack space.\n\nA concise implementation is shown in the detailed answer.",
    detailedAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nUse recursion to remove the top element until the stack is empty. Then insert each removed element at the bottom while the recursive calls return. The key helper is insertAtBottom, which temporarily removes elements until the bottom is reached. This uses O(n2) time in the straightforward implementation and O(n) call-stack space.\n\n**Implementation example:**\n\n```python\ndef insert_bottom(stack, x):\n    if not stack:\n        stack.append(x)\n        return\n    top = stack.pop()\n    insert_bottom(stack, x)\n    stack.append(top)\n\ndef reverse_stack(stack):\n    if not stack:\n        return\n    top = stack.pop()\n    reverse_stack(stack)\n    insert_bottom(stack, top)\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\nPush 5, then 2, then 7 into a min-stack. getMin() returns 2; after popping 7 it remains 2, and after popping 2 it returns to 5. The example is deliberately focused on the specific interview topic in entry 21.",
